## Summary

**No Zimmermann override exists for any part of this flow.** Every file involved in "Add to Wishlist" / duplicate-add handling is 100% unmodified `@salesforce/retail-react-app` v10.0.0 code. I verified this by searching `overrides/app` for every filename pattern that could plausibly touch this flow (`*wishlist*`, `*item-variant*`, `*cart-secondary*`, `*use-wish-list*`, `cart/`, `product-detail/`, `product-list/`, `*product-item-list*`, `*product-tile*`, `*mini-cart*`) — all returned zero matches. The only "wishlist" hits inside `overrides/` are unrelated (a nav link in `overrides/app/components/header/index.tsx`, compiled i18n JSON, a Chakra theme file). `overrides/app/constants/index.ts` does `export * from '@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/constants'` and only adds `CUSTOM_HOME_TITLE` plus re-exports of home-page cache constants — it does not touch the wishlist toast strings.

So: **the answer to the business question is simply "what does native SFCC PWA Kit do," unmodified.**

## What actually happens (native template behavior, currently live)

**Item stays in the cart — always, in every case (success, duplicate, or error).**

The Cart page's "Add to Wishlist" button and the "Remove" button are two independent, sibling actions. Clicking "Add to Wishlist" never triggers item removal:

- `node_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/pages/cart/partials/cart-secondary-button-group.jsx:93-104` — the button (labelled **"Add to Wishlist"**, not "Move to Wishlist", `id: cart_secondary_button_group.action.added_to_wishlist`) only calls `onAddToWishlistClick(variant)`:
  ```jsx
  <Button variant="link" size="sm" onClick={() => onAddToWishlistClick(variant)}>
      <FormattedMessage defaultMessage="Add to Wishlist" .../>
  </Button>
  ```
- The separate "Remove" button (lines 87-92) is wired to its own confirmation-modal flow (`showRemoveItemConfirmation` → `handleRemoveItem` → `onRemoveItemClick(variant)`), completely decoupled from the wishlist action.
- In the parent, `node_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/pages/cart/index.jsx:991-1002` wires `onAddToWishlistClick={handleAddToWishlist}`, and `handleAddToWishlist` (lines 422-475) **never calls `removeItemFromBasketMutation` or `handleRemoveItem`** anywhere in its body.

**Shopper sees a message either way — never silent, and duplicate is not treated as an error:**

The dedupe/toast logic, `cart/index.jsx:416-476`:
```js
const {data: wishlist} = useWishList()
const createCustomerProductListItem = useShopperCustomersMutation('createCustomerProductListItem')
const handleAddToWishlist = async (product) => {
    try {
        if (!customerId || !wishlist) {
            return
        }
        const isItemInWishlist = wishlist?.customerProductListItems?.find(
            (i) => i.productId === product?.id
        )
        if (!isItemInWishlist) {
            await createCustomerProductListItem.mutateAsync({...body: {quantity: product.quantity, productId: product.productId, public: false, priority: 1, type: 'product'}})
            toast({ title: formatMessage(TOAST_MESSAGE_ADDED_TO_WISHLIST, {quantity: 1}), status: 'success', action: <Button.../> })
        } else {
            toast({ title: formatMessage(TOAST_MESSAGE_ALREADY_IN_WISHLIST), status: 'info', action: <Button.../> })
        }
    } catch {
        showError()   // generic API_ERROR_MESSAGE toast, status: 'error'
    }
}
```
(cart/index.jsx:422-475; `showError` defined at cart/index.jsx:408-413)

- **This is client-side dedupe, not reliance on the SFCC API to reject a duplicate.** The check `wishlist?.customerProductListItems?.find((i) => i.productId === product?.id)` runs against the already-cached wishlist (from `useWishList()`, `node_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/hooks/use-wish-list.js:13-42`) *before* the mutation fires. If a match is found, `createCustomerProductListItem.mutateAsync` (the Shopper Customers `POST .../product-lists/{listId}/items` call) is **never invoked** — so the SFCC API is never given the chance to accept or reject the duplicate.
- On duplicate: toast `status: 'info'`, title = `TOAST_MESSAGE_ALREADY_IN_WISHLIST` = **"Item is already in wishlist"** (`node_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/constants.js:128-131`), with a "View" action button that navigates to `/account/wishlist` (`TOAST_ACTION_VIEW_WISHLIST`, constants.js:138-141). Not an error toast, not a success toast — an informational one.
- On success (not a duplicate): toast `status: 'success'`, title = `TOAST_MESSAGE_ADDED_TO_WISHLIST` = **"{quantity} items added to wishlist"** (constants.js:123-126), same "View" action.
- On a genuine failure (network/API error during the actual create call): the `catch` block fires `showError()` → `status: 'error'`, title = `API_ERROR_MESSAGE`. This path is unreachable for the duplicate scenario specifically, since duplicates short-circuit before the API call.

## Identical pattern on PDP, different pattern on PLP

- **PDP** (`node_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/pages/product-detail/index.jsx:244-301`) has the exact same `isItemInWishlist` guard/toast structure (mutation skipped, `TOAST_MESSAGE_ALREADY_IN_WISHLIST` info toast shown instead).
- **PLP** (`node_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/pages/product-list/index.jsx:248-292`) does *not* have this in-function guard. Instead the duplicate case is prevented one layer up in the UI: `isInWishlist` is computed at product-list/index.jsx:612-615 and fed into `<ProductTile isFavourite={isInWishlist} onFavouriteToggle={(toBeFavourite) => (toBeFavourite ? addItemToWishlist : removeItemFromWishlist)(...)} .../>` (~line 649-655) — clicking an already-active star calls `removeItemFromWishlist`, not `addItemToWishlist`. Not directly relevant to the cart question, but shows the app isn't 100% consistent in *how* it prevents duplicate adds (function-level guard vs. UI-level toggle) — only worth flagging if you want consistency across surfaces.

## Test/Storybook coverage

- **No test exists for this scenario in the Cart page.** `node_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/pages/cart/index.test.js` has zero mentions of "wishlist" (confirmed via case-insensitive grep). `cart/partials/cart-secondary-button-group.test.js` only asserts that clicking "Add to Wishlist" invokes the passed-in mock callback — it never exercises the real `handleAddToWishlist` dedupe/toast logic (that logic lives one level up, in `cart/index.jsx`, untested).
- **A passing test does exist for the identical logic on PDP**, and it directly encodes the expected behavior: `node_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/pages/product-detail/index.test.js:232-256`, test name `'should not add to wishlist if item is already in wishlist'`:
  ```js
  test('should not add to wishlist if item is already in wishlist', async () => {
      global.server.use(
          rest.get('*/products/:productId', (req, res, ctx) => res(ctx.json(masterProduct))),
          rest.get('*/customers/:customerId/product-lists', (req, res, ctx) =>
              res(ctx.delay(0), ctx.status(200), ctx.json(mockWishlistWithItem))
          )
      )
      renderWithProviders(<MockedComponent />)
      ...
      const wishlistButton = await screen.findByRole('button', {name: 'Add to Wishlist'})
      fireEvent.click(wishlistButton)
      await waitFor(() => {
          expect(mockAddToWishlist).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(0)
      })
  })
  ```
  This confirms, via assertion, that the mutate function is called **zero times** when the wishlist already contains the item — i.e., the "no API call, client-side dedupe" behavior is intentional and verified, at least for PDP.
- **No Storybook `.stories.*` file matching "wishlist" exists anywhere in the repo**, including inside `node_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app` — none found.
- Only two other wishlist-related test files exist in the base template, both unrelated to this duplicate-add question: `pages/account/wishlist/partials/wishlist-primary-action.test.js` and `wishlist-secondary-button-group.test.js` (the reverse "move to bag" flow on the wishlist page itself), and `hooks/use-bonus-product-selection-modal/use-bonus-product-wishlist.test.js` (bonus-product-specific wishlist add, same pattern, different feature).
- Test runner confirmed as **Vitest** (`package.json:45`, `"test": "vitest run"`), consistent with the task's framing, even though the base template's own spec files use Jest-style syntax (Vitest is Jest-API-compatible).

## PRD note worth flagging to the Frontend Lead

`.docs/prd/cart.md:11-12` and `:23-24` describe this action as **"Move to Wishlist"** ("Actions per line item: Move to Wishlist, Remove" — CAI-004/CAI-008), and `.docs/memory/projectState.md:126` also uses "Move-to-Wishlist" terminology. But the shipped/native code labels the button **"Add to Wishlist"** (`cart-secondary-button-group.jsx:99-102`, i18n id `cart_secondary_button_group.action.added_to_wishlist`) and, as shown above, never removes the item from the cart under any circumstance — duplicate or not. Nothing in `.docs/prd/` or `.docs/integration/` specifically documents the duplicate-add case itself (no doc says what should happen when the item is already wishlisted); the PRD is silent on that specific sub-behavior. So if "Move to Wishlist" (remove-on-success semantics) is the actual business intent, that would require new custom code in `overrides/` — today it doesn't exist, and the live behavior is copy-only, duplicate-safe, cart-item-preserving "Add to Wishlist."

